<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue name="Chaos - Dark Mechanicum" id="6f50-c084-6764-e3cc" authorContact="Centuria Astartes Discord, ask for AHeras." authorName="A. Heras" authorUrl="Centuria Astartes Discord" battleScribeVersion="2.03" gameSystemId="5b78-3a13-0882-b019" gameSystemRevision="4" library="false" revision="2" type="catalogue" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <readme>Well, let&apos;s see what happens next.</readme>
  <categoryEntries>
    <categoryEntry name="Heretek Cult" id="ccbe-78a9-3dd8-7cf7" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Silica Animus" id="c4d0-57e3-9d5a-6905" hidden="true" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Models with this ability can re-roll armour Saving throws of 1 and can ignore any or all modifiers to the Hit roll.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="5d6c-12da-407d-ff32" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                        <condition childId="5d6c-12da-407d-ff32" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="48fb-77b6-266b-6502" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Empyrea Chronodisruptors" id="dbaa-70e8-2bbc-6e71" hidden="true" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Models with this ability regain 1 wound in each Command phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="6167-0b15-2ece-6673" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Bound testing" id="6f37-1b6a-3357-3e42" hidden="true">
          <comment>Dark Mechanicum</comment>
          <description>In your Command phase, you can select to push the bounds, or keep within know parameters.

In case of Push, roll a 1D6, if the result is greater than the current Battle round, HERETEK CULT units from your army receive a Push Bonus ability as shown in the following table. Those abilities are cumulative.
If the result is equal or lesser than the current Battle round, HERETEK CULT units from your army gain the corresponding ability from the Out of Bounds ability table. If you already have the corresponding ability, no Out of Bounds ability is gained.
						
Push Bonus
1st- 		HERETEK CULT units ignore Movement modifiers due to Difficult Ground, and add 2&quot; to Advance and Charge rolls.
2nd-		HERETEK CULT units can Advance and Charge in the same turn.
3rd-		HERETEK CULT units add 1 to Invulnerable Saving throws.
4th-		HERETEK CULT units add 1 to rolls regarding Abilities that allow prevent Wound loses.
5th-		HERETEK CULT units are considered to have be Remained Stationary during the Psychic, Shooting and Charge phases, even if a unit have made a Normal Move, Advanced, Fell back or Disembarked during the previous Movement Phase.
6th-		HERETEK CULT units can re-roll Invulnerable Saving throws.

Roll	Out of Bounds Malus
1-	HERETEK CULT units, when making an attack, must re-roll wounds rolls of 6.
2-	HERETEK CULT units cannot be affected by friendly Aura abilities.
3-	HERETEK CULT units cannot re-roll the Hit roll, irrespective of any abilities that the weapon or the unit may have.
4-	HERETEK CULT units are always considered to be in Difficult Ground.
5-	HERETEK CULT units, when receiving a Stratagem, must first roll 2D6, if the result is less than the Leadership characteristic of the unit, the Stratagem has no effect on that unit.
6-	HERETEK CULT units reduce their Leadership characteristic by 1.</description>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="2d09-dec9-0451-4187" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Adaptative approach" id="2f7d-e197-52de-a7b1" hidden="true">
          <comment>Heretek Cults</comment>
          <description>At the beginning of the first Battle Round and in each of your Command phases, generate Evolution points for your army as follows:
- If you choose to Adapt within parameters, roll a 1D3 and add the current Battle round to the result.
- If you choose to Push, roll a 1D6, and add the current Battle round number to the result.
Once the Evolution points have been calculated, choose one ability with an equal value or lesser than your Evolution points from the Adaptation abilities table. Until the end of the battle HERETEK CULT units from your army gain the chosen Adaptation ability.
If you have chosen to Push to the limit, HERETEK CULT units from your army gain the corresponding ability from the Out of Bounds ability table. If you already have the corresponding ability, no Out of Bounds ability is gained.
Any unspent Evolution points are lost.

EP	Adaptation Table
1- 	HERETEK CULT units automatically pass Morale Tests on a roll of 6.
2- 	HERETEK CULT units ignore Movement modifiers due to Difficult Ground.
3- 	HERETEK CULT units add 2&quot; to Advance and Charge rolls.
4- 	HERETEK CULT units can Fall back and Shoot in the same turn.
5- 	HERETEK CULT units can Advance and Charge in the same turn.
6- 	HERETEK CULT units can Fight first during the Fight phase.
7- 	HERETEK CULT units add 1 to rolls regarding Abilities that allow prevent Wound loses.
8- 	HERETEK CULT units are considered to have be Remained Stationary during the Psychic, Shooting and Charge phases, even if a unit have made a Normal Move, Advanced, Fell back or Disembarked during the previous Movement Phase.
9- 	HERETEK CULT units can re-roll Invulnerable Saving throws.
10- 	HERETEK CULT units can re-roll rolls regarding Abilities that allow prevent Wound loses.

Roll	Out of Bounds Malus
1-	HERETEK CULT units, when making an attack, must re-roll wounds rolls of 6.
2-	HERETEK CULT units cannot be affected by friendly Aura abilities.
3-	HERETEK CULT units cannot re-roll the Hit roll, irrespective of any abilities that the weapon or the unit may have.
4-	HERETEK CULT units are always considered to be in Difficult Ground.
5-	HERETEK CULT units, when receiving a Stratagem, must first roll 2D6, if the result is less than the Leadership characteristic of the unit, the Stratagem has no effect on that unit.
6-	HERETEK CULT units reduce their Leadership characteristic by 1.</description>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="11b9-32f1-0c64-01e2" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Heretek Tech Priest" id="aa46-9fe9-320e-8d3e" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Master of Technology" id="8849-0650-b497-7166" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">At the end of your Movement phase, this model can repair one friendly &lt;HERETEK&gt; model or a friendly VEHICLE model within 3&quot; of it. That model regains up to D3 lost wounds. Each model can only be repaired once per turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Sonic weapon" id="91db-06e9-d620-363a" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Sonic weapon" id="1d81-eaf0-da1b-c882" hidden="false">
          <description>Each time an attack made with this weapon targets a unit within half range, add 1 to the Damage characteristic of that attack.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Plage weapon" id="6d64-6f9d-33e2-b972" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Plage weapon" id="d82b-0672-754e-8e97" hidden="false">
          <description>Re-roll wound rolls of 1 against units without the VEHICLE, TITANIC or INORGANIC Keywords.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Daemon Engine" id="c6b2-ced1-346e-464b" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Possessed" id="6d64-0a46-e00a-3482" hidden="false">
      <comment>d16b-0a7c-0494-a2a4</comment>
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Posessed" id="f366-7587-9ad5-840c" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">If your army includes a POSESSED unit in the battlefield during one of your Command phases, check if it becomes Unleashed, by rolling a D6, becoming unleashed if the roll is lesser orr equal to the current Battle Round.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="c8fd-783f-3230-493e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="c8fd-783f-3230-493e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Posessed unleashed" id="328d-8f29-5fcf-24ce" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">- If a POSESSED unit without the CHARACTER Keyword becomes unleashed, in each Movement phase unless in engagement range of enemy units, it cannot Remain Stationary, it must Advance against the nearest visible enemy unit, and it can Advance and Charge in the same turn.
- Unleashed POSESSED units must charge if they can, and always against the nearest able enemy unit.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Posessed" id="5a5c-cf74-7a08-1062" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <comment>Vehicle</comment>
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">- If your army includes a POSESSED unit in the battlefield during one of your Command phases, check if it becomes Unleashed, by rolling a D6, becoming unleashed if the roll is lesser orr equal to the current Battle Round.
- Each time a Posessed VEHICLE kills an enemy miniature with a melee attack, can attack one time more, this attacks cannot generate more attacks.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="c8fd-783f-3230-493e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="c8fd-783f-3230-493e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="notInstanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Phosphor weapon." id="eece-8ef4-ea28-175b" hidden="false"/>
  </categoryEntries>
